From a2e75036ccb8d74c324f1a33fa7e67f3c7e2305b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raza <raza@bukc.edu.pk>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 10:56:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): lockout counter never reset after expiry, causing
 effectively indefinite lock
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Real bug, not a stale UI message — confirmed and reproduced against a
real database before fixing.

failed_login_count was only ever reset to 0 on a SUCCESSFUL login. Once
an account crossed the 5-failure threshold and got locked for 15
minutes, that counter stayed frozen at 5 for as long as the account kept
failing to log in — which meant the very next wrong-password attempt
after the lock naturally expired computed nextCount = 5 + 1 = 6 (still
>= the threshold), silently re-locking for another full 15-minute
window. This repeats on every subsequent attempt that isn't the correct
password, so in practice a locked account stays locked indefinitely
unless the very first attempt after each expiry happens to be correct.

Fix: when a login request arrives for an account whose locked_until has
genuinely passed, that's treated as a fresh start — the counter resets
to 0 (and locked_until clears) before this attempt is evaluated, so a
wrong guess right after expiry counts as failure #1, not #6.

Reproduced the exact bug against a live database with a standalone
script before writing the fix (5 failures -> simulate expiry -> one more
wrong guess -> confirmed it immediately re-locked under the old code's
logic), then confirmed the fix resolves it the same way.

Also, per direct request: locked accounts are now visible in the Active
Accounts admin screen. AUTH-11 lockouts are informational metadata on
top of ACTIVE status (a locked account isn't deactivated, it just can't
log in for a bit) — added lockedUntil to the ManagedAccount shape
(listActiveAccounts, searchAccounts, getMyProfile), server-side filtered
to only ever surface it while still actually in effect (an expired lock
is stale data cleared lazily on next login attempt, not proactively, so
the API doesn't present it as if it were current). Client: a new
'Locked' badge appears next to the status pill in both the account list
row and the click-through detail modal, with a hover tooltip explaining
what triggered it and the exact unlock time.

Tests: T-108b reproduces the exact reported bug end-to-end through the
real HTTP/service layer (5 failures, simulate expiry, one more wrong
guess must NOT re-lock, counter must read exactly 1, correct password
must then work) — this is the regression test that would have caught
the original bug. T-144 confirms lockedUntil surfaces correctly in both
the Active Accounts list and search while a lock is genuinely active,
and disappears once it's expired.

Verified against a real local Postgres: tsc --noEmit clean on both
sides, production build clean, full suite — all 7 files, 151/151 tests
— passes.
